#31: 
Downgrade the requirements passed to the allocator in the gfp flags parameter.

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*auxbuf)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct cachefiles_xattr)...)
#192: FILE: fs/cachefiles/xattr.c:177:
+	auxbuf = kmalloc(sizeof(struct cachefiles_xattr) + 512, cachefiles_gfp);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

